I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. An `http-client` import would exceed that grant even with the platform team's approval. The fetch would also send raw input text into a URL query string, which is an injection and data-exposure risk. Adding it needs a grant change in the graph definition, not a change to this crate.

The crate below implements the node as declared. It reads the `subscriptions` key from state, which holds one URL per line, and returns an empty list if the key is absent.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = state_read::get("subscriptions")
            .map(|raw| {
                raw.lines()
                    .map(str::trim)
                    .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                    .map(String::from)
                    .collect::<Vec<String>>()
            })
            .unwrap_or_default();

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

